# Toggle state persistence

The card currently uses:

```javascript
sessionStorage
```

for remembering switch states during the session.

The intended logic is:

```javascript
const defaultStates = {
  "show-flags": true,
  "show-1-2": false,
  "show-3-6": true
};
```

Retrieval:

```javascript
function getStoredState(id) {

  try {

    const stored =
      sessionStorage.getItem(id);

    if (stored === null) {
      return defaultStates[id];
    }

    return stored === "true";

  }

  catch (error) {

    return defaultStates[id];

  }

}
```

Saving:

```javascript
function saveState(id, state) {

  try {

    sessionStorage.setItem(
      id,
      String(state)
    );

  }

  catch (error) {

    /* Storage unavailable */

  }

}
```

The switch state should then control classes on:

```javascript
const card =
  document.getElementById("anki-card");
```

using:

```javascript
card.classList.toggle(
  "show-flags",
  showFlags
);

card.classList.toggle(
  "show-bottom-fields",
  showBottom
);

card.classList.toggle(
  "show-top-fields",
  showTop
);
```

