# Edge SpeechSynthesis version

For the browser version, do NOT use:

```html
{{tts ...}}
```

Instead use the browser Web Speech API:

```javascript
SpeechSynthesisUtterance
```

and:

```javascript
speechSynthesis.getVoices()
```

The goal is primarily Microsoft Edge.

I want the browser to prefer Microsoft Edge Online / Natural voices where available.

Target locales:

```text
English UK:
en-GB

German:
de-DE

Norwegian Bokmål:
nb-NO

Spanish Spain:
es-ES
```

Preferred voice families can include:

```text
English:
Sonia
Ryan

German:
Katja
Conrad

Norwegian:
Pernille
Finn
Iselin

Spanish:
Elvira
Alvaro
```

Do not assume exact names will always exist.

The code should dynamically inspect:

```javascript
speechSynthesis.getVoices()
```

and choose the best matching voice.

Preferred selection priority:

1. Correct locale
2. Preferred voice name
3. Name contains `Natural`
4. Name contains `Online`
5. Any voice matching the locale
6. Browser default as last fallback

Example conceptual function:

```javascript
function findVoice(locale) {

  const localeVoices =
    availableVoices.filter(function (voice) {

      return voice.lang.toLowerCase() ===
             locale.toLowerCase();

    });

  // Prefer matching Online/Natural voice,
  // otherwise fall back to any locale voice.

}
```

Playback:

```javascript
function speakText(text, locale) {

  speechSynthesis.cancel();

  const utterance =
    new SpeechSynthesisUtterance(text);

  utterance.lang = locale;

  const voice =
    findVoice(locale);

  if (voice) {
    utterance.voice = voice;
  }

  utterance.rate = 1;
  utterance.pitch = 1;
  utterance.volume = 1;

  speechSynthesis.speak(utterance);

}
```

The black circular play buttons should trigger this function.

Example:

```javascript
speakText(
  "Jeg ønsker å forbedre uttalen min hver dag.",
  "nb-NO"
);
```

