# Separate list-parser Anki card

There is also another related Anki card in this project that parses a compact list format.

Its data format is:

```text
audio1↑text1a↑text1b↓audio2↑text2a↑text2b↓audio3↑text3a↑text3b
```

Parsing rules:

```text
↓ = row delimiter
↑ = column delimiter
```

Columns:

```text
column 1 = audio
column 2 = Field 1 / text A
column 3 = Field 2 / text B
```

Parser:

```javascript
const items = raw
  .split("↓")
  .map(item => item.trim())
  .filter(Boolean)
  .map(item => {

    const [
      soundAudio = "",
      contentText = "",
      contentText2 = ""
    ] = item.split("↑");

    return {
      soundAudio: soundAudio.trim(),
      contentText: contentText.trim(),
      contentText2: contentText2.trim()
    };

  });
```

The order MUST remain sequential.

Do not randomize.

---

# List-parser navigation

Current navigation logic uses:

```text
9 = next
8 = previous
P = reset
```

A `Ctrl+8` shortcut can also be intercepted before plain `8`.

Important ordering:

```javascript
if (key === "9") {

  event.preventDefault();

  window.showNextItem();

} else if (event.ctrlKey && key === "8") {

  event.preventDefault();

  window.resetItems();

} else if (key === "8") {

  event.preventDefault();

  window.showPreviousItem();

} else if (key === "p") {

  event.preventDefault();

  window.resetItems();

}
```

Because `Ctrl+8` also satisfies:

```javascript
key === "8"
```

the Ctrl condition MUST appear first.

